[quotes.thriving]
Fully corporeal and thrilled about it.
Solid enough to hold a bookmark today.
Ooooo. That is a joyful noise, not a spooky one.
Reading keeps me here. No pressure.
I have never felt so gloriously undead.
Look at me go. Practically got a pulse.
The most alive a dead thing can feel.
Keep this up and I will start paying rent.

[quotes.content]
Drifting pleasantly over your shoulder.
Just enough pages to keep me opaque.
I am not haunting you. I am supervising.
A quiet day. I approve of quiet.
Semi-transparent, semi-content. It works.
Do not mind the cold spot. That is just me.
I have seen worse readers. All dead now.
Steady. Spectral. Satisfied.

[quotes.peckish]
Getting a little thin around the edges.
Can you still see me? Be honest.
I appear to be going translucent. Rude.
One more page would firm me right up.
Bloody hell, I can see through my own hands.
Do not let me become a rumour.
I am fading and you are not reading. Cool.
This is how ghosts die. Twice.

[quotes.neglected]
Barely here. Mostly vapour and regret.
I have sunk to the floor. This is my life now.
Boo. That is all I have left in me.
Fading. Tell the books I said hello.
Well. Shit. I think this is the actual end.
Forgotten twice. That is a hell of a record.
I died once. This is somehow worse.
No flowers, please. I cannot hold them.

[quotes.milestone]
A new record. I have never felt so solid.
Best streak yet. I might survive this century.
Look at me, practically alive. Well done you.
New personal best. The dead are impressed.
